{
    "map": {
        "area_of_interest.descr": "A feature layer that will be used to clip the input raster before processing. A buffer is created before clipping the raster, which results in larger output contours that extend beyond the selected area of interest. The feature layer must have only one selected feature.",
        "area_of_interest.title": "Area of Interest",
        "base_contour.descr": "The value that contours will be generated above and below to cover the entire value range of the input raster. The default is 0.",
        "base_contour.title": "Base Contour",
        "code_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>The field from the input contour feature class where the appropriate code will be stored. The default field is <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">HQC</span> if it exists in the input contour feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "code_field.title": "Contour Code Field",
        "contour_features.descr": "An existing line feature class or feature layer. Contours will be appended to this feature class.",
        "contour_features.title": "Target Contour Features",
        "contour_interval.descr": "The interval, or distance, between contour lines. This can be any positive number. The default is set by the scale value. If this parameter is left blank, the default scale value will be used.",
        "contour_interval.title": "Contour Interval",
        "contour_smooth_tolerance.descr": "The amount of smoothing that will be applied to the contour lines. The larger the value, the more generalized the contours. The default is set by the scale value. If this parameter is set to 0 or left blank, no smoothing will be applied to the output contours.",
        "contour_smooth_tolerance.title": "Contour Smooth Tolerance",
        "contour_subtype.descr": "The subtype to which contours will be written if the input contours have subtypes.",
        "contour_subtype.title": "Contour Subtype",
        "depression_auxiliary_code.descr": "<xdoc><p>The code value that will be stored in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Contour Code Field</span> parameter value when a depression auxiliary contour is identified. The default code is 22 if the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">HQC</span> field exists in the input contour feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "depression_auxiliary_code.title": "Depression Auxiliary Code",
        "depression_code.descr": "<xdoc><p>The code value that will be stored in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Contour Code Field</span> parameter value when a depression contour is identified. The default code is 5 if the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">HQC</span> field exists in the input contour feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "depression_code.title": "Depression Code",
        "depression_intermediate_code.descr": "<xdoc><p>The code value that will be stored in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Contour Code Field</span> parameter value when a depression intermediate contour is identified. The default code is 6 if the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">HQC</span> field exists in the input contour feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "depression_intermediate_code.title": "Depression Intermediate Code",
        "description": "Creates and smooths contours from an input raster.",
        "elevation_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>The field from the input contours that will store the contour elevation value. This field defaults to <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">ZV2</span> or <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">ZVH</span> if a field with either of those names exists in the contour feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "elevation_field.title": "Contour Elevation Field",
        "half_auxiliary_code.descr": "<xdoc><p>The code value that will be stored in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Contour Code Field</span> parameter value when a half auxiliary contour is identified. The default code is 3 if the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">HQC</span> field exists in the input contour feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "half_auxiliary_code.title": "Half Auxiliary Code",
        "in_rasters.descr": "The input raster layers that will be used to derive the contour lines.",
        "in_rasters.title": "Input Rasters",
        "index_code.descr": "<xdoc><p>The code value that will be stored in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Contour Code Field</span> parameter value when an index contour is identified. The default code is 1 if the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">HQC</span> field exists in the input contour feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "index_code.title": "Index Code",
        "index_interval.descr": "The interval, or distance, between index contour lines. For example, if the contour interval is 20 meters and you want index contours every 100 meters, specify 100. The default is set by the scale value.",
        "index_interval.title": "Contour Index Interval",
        "intermediate_code.descr": "<xdoc><p>The code value that will be stored in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Contour Code Field</span> parameter value when an intermediate contour is identified. The default code is 2 if the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">HQC</span> field exists in the input contour feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "intermediate_code.title": "Intermediate Code",
        "minimum_length.descr": "The minimum length that will be used for an individual contour line. The default is set by the scale value. If the value is set to 0 or left blank, no contours will be deleted from the output contours based on their short length.",
        "minimum_length.title": "Contour Minimum Length",
        "params.category1": "Elevation Values",
        "params.category2": "Contour Codes",
        "params.category3": "Contour Refinement",
        "params.category4": "Supplemental Contour Codes",
        "quarter_auxiliary_code.descr": "<xdoc><p>The code value that will be stored in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Contour Code Field</span> parameter value when a quarter auxiliary contour is identified. The default code is 14 if the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">HQC</span> field exists in the input contour feature class</p></xdoc>",
        "quarter_auxiliary_code.title": "Quarter Auxiliary Code",
        "raster_smooth_tolerance.descr": "The amount of smoothing that will be applied to the input raster before creating the contour lines.",
        "raster_smooth_tolerance.title": "Raster Smooth Tolerance",
        "resample_raster.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether the input raster will be resampled before creating contours.</p><ul><li>Checked—The input raster will be resampled before creating contours.</li><li>Unchecked—The input raster will not be resampled when creating contours. This is the default.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "resample_raster.title": "Resample Raster",
        "scale.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the scale that will be used to optimize contours. This is the scale of the cartographic product that will be printed. Specifying the scale will set the defaults of other parameters to values that are appropriate for the output scale. The default is 1:50,000.</p><ul><li><span title=\"1:5,000\">1:5,000</span>—The 1:5,000 cartographic product scale will be used.</li><li><span title=\"1:10,000\">1:10,000</span>—The 1:10,000 cartographic product scale will be used.</li><li><span title=\"1:12,500\">1:12,500</span>—The 1:12,500 cartographic product scale will be used.</li><li><span title=\"1:25,000\">1:25,000</span>—The 1:25,000 cartographic product scale will be used.</li><li><span title=\"1:50,000\">1:50,000</span>—The 1:50,000 cartographic product scale will be used. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"1:100,000\">1:100,000</span>—The 1:100,000 cartographic product scale will be used.</li><li><span title=\"1:250,000\">1:250,000</span>—The 1:250,000 cartographic product scale will be used.</li><li><span title=\"1:500,000\">1:500,000</span>—The 1:500,000 cartographic product scale will be used.</li><li><span title=\"1:1,000,000\">1:1,000,000</span>—The 1:1,000,000 cartographic product scale will be used.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "scale.domain. ": " ",
        "scale.domain.1:1,000,000": "1:1,000,000",
        "scale.domain.1:10,000": "1:10,000",
        "scale.domain.1:100,000": "1:100,000",
        "scale.domain.1:12,500": "1:12,500",
        "scale.domain.1:25,000": "1:25,000",
        "scale.domain.1:250,000": "1:250,000",
        "scale.domain.1:5,000": "1:5,000",
        "scale.domain.1:50,000": "1:50,000",
        "scale.domain.1:500,000": "1:500,000",
        "scale.title": "Map Scale",
        "supplemental_contours.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the interval at which a contour line will be placed between regularly spaced contours. This is used when the terrain change is not large enough to be depicted with consistent contour intervals.</p><ul><li><span title=\"NONE\">None</span>—No supplemental contours will be created. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"HALF_AUXILIARY\">Half Auxiliary</span>—Supplemental contours will be created at one-half the contour interval.</li><li><span title=\"QUARTER_AUXILIARY\">Quarter Auxiliary</span>—Supplemental contours will be created at one-quarter the contour interval.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "supplemental_contours.domain.HALF_AUXILIARY": "Half Auxiliary",
        "supplemental_contours.domain.NONE": "None",
        "supplemental_contours.domain.QUARTER_AUXILIARY": "Quarter Auxiliary",
        "supplemental_contours.title": "Supplemental Contours",
        "title": "Generate Topographic Contours",
        "updated_contour_features.title": "Updated Contour Features",
        "z_factor.descr": "<xdoc><p>The unit conversion factor that will be used when generating contours. The default is 1.</p><p>The contour lines are generated based on the z-values in the input raster, which are often measured in units of meters or feet. With the default value of 1, the contours will be in the same units as the z-values of the input raster. To create contours in a unit other than that of the z-values, set an appropriate value for the z-factor. It is not necessary that the ground x,y and surface z-units be consistent for this tool.</p><p>For example, if the elevation values in the input raster are in meters but you want the contours to be generated in feet, set the z-factor to 3.28084 (1 meter = 3.28084 feet).</p></xdoc>",
        "z_factor.title": "Z Factor",
        "zero_contour.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether a zero contour will be created. A zero contour represents sea level. Zero contours, when generated along a coastline, may be created inside a water body. Check this parameter if you want contours generated on land areas that are at or below sea level.</p><ul><li>Checked—A zero contour will be created.</li><li>Unchecked—A zero contour will not be created. This is the default.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "zero_contour.title": "Include Zero Contour"
    }
}
